<section
  id="paradigm"
  class="paradigm section"
  aria-labelledby="paradigm-title"
>
  <div class="paradigm-atmosphere" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="container-wide paradigm-container">
    <header class="paradigm-header">
      <p class="paradigm-eyebrow">THE ALEPH PARADIGM</p>

      <h2 id="paradigm-title">
        <span class="paradigm-title-main">
          Intelligence is not a component.
        </span>
        <span class="paradigm-title-accent">
          It is an engineered system.
        </span>
      </h2>

      <div class="paradigm-thesis" aria-label="Aleph architecture summary">
        <span class="thesis-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>DETERMINISTIC SOFTWARE</span>
        <span class="thesis-plus">+</span>
        <span>PROBABILISTIC AI</span>
        <span class="thesis-plus">+</span>
        <span>AGENTS</span>
        <span class="thesis-plus">+</span>
        <span>GOVERNANCE</span>
      </div>

      <p class="paradigm-intro">
        Aleph Innovation does not treat an LLM as the application. We engineer
        systems in which deterministic software, probabilistic models and
        specialized agents operate inside explicit contracts, evidence
        boundaries and validation gates.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div
      class="paradigm-architecture"
      aria-label="Aleph Innovation Agentic AI architecture"
    >
      <article class="architecture-node deterministic">
        <div class="node-header">
          <span class="node-index">01</span>
          <span class="node-type">CONTROL</span>
        </div>

        <h3>Deterministic Core</h3>

        <p>
          Numerical computation, constraints, contracts, state transitions
          and business rules remain explicit, reproducible and testable.
        </p>

        <div class="node-tags">
          <span>Python</span>
          <span>Contracts</span>
          <span>Validation</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="architecture-connector" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="connector-label">CONTEXT</span>
        <span class="connector-line"></span>
        <span class="connector-arrow">→</span>
      </div>

      <article class="architecture-node probabilistic">
        <div class="node-header">
          <span class="node-index">02</span>
          <span class="node-type">REASONING</span>
        </div>

        <h3>Probabilistic AI</h3>

        <p>
          Language models interpret evidence, extract semantic factors,
          generate hypotheses and reason over information that cannot be
          reduced to deterministic rules alone.
        </p>

        <div class="node-tags">
          <span>LLMs</span>
          <span>Research</span>
          <span>Inference</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="architecture-connector" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="connector-label">DELEGATE</span>
        <span class="connector-line"></span>
        <span class="connector-arrow">→</span>
      </div>

      <article class="architecture-node agents">
        <div class="node-header">
          <span class="node-index">03</span>
          <span class="node-type">AGENCY</span>
        </div>

        <h3>Specialized Agents</h3>

        <p>
          Multiple agents can investigate different dimensions of a problem,
          challenge assumptions and produce competing assessments rather than
          collapsing reasoning into a single model response.
        </p>

        <div class="agent-mini-network" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>A</span>
          <span>B</span>
          <span>C</span>
        </div>

        <div class="node-tags">
          <span>Specialization</span>
          <span>Competition</span>
          <span>Consensus</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="architecture-connector" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="connector-label">VERIFY</span>
        <span class="connector-line"></span>
        <span class="connector-arrow">→</span>
      </div>

      <article class="architecture-node governance">
        <div class="node-header">
          <span class="node-index">04</span>
          <span class="node-type">GOVERNANCE</span>
        </div>

        <h3>Validation &amp; Decision</h3>

        <p>
          Evidence quality, confidence, portfolio constraints and system
          invariants are evaluated before an AI recommendation can influence
          a real-world decision.
        </p>

        <div class="node-tags">
          <span>Evidence</span>
          <span>Gates</span>
          <span>Human Authority</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="paradigm-loop" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="loop-rail"></span>
      <span class="loop-label">
        OBSERVE <b>·</b> TEST <b>·</b> CHALLENGE <b>·</b> VALIDATE <b>·</b> LEARN
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="paradigm-principle">
      <div class="principle-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
      </div>

      <p class="principle-label">DESIGN PRINCIPLE</p>

      <div class="principle-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <p class="principle-statement">
        Use deterministic software where certainty is possible.
        Use probabilistic AI where interpretation is necessary.
        Use agents where independent reasoning creates value.
        <strong>
          Never confuse probabilistic output with verified truth.
        </strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

